# 10. M2.1 — Important Defect Found During Review

The first implementation review identified a potential stale file registry entry.

## 10.1 Stale pointer problem

Suppose:

```text
Memfd A
  |
  v
struct file F1
  |
  v
memfd_file_registry[F1] = token_A
```

When F1 reaches its final release, its memory may eventually be reused.

If the map entry remains:

```text
memfd_file_registry[F1] = token_A
```

A future unrelated file might occupy the same kernel memory address.

A lookup could then incorrectly associate an unrelated file with Memfd A.

This would be a serious forensic false-attribution problem.

## 10.2 Required distinction

The cleanup must remove the `struct file *` entry without retiring the backing object.

`__fput` was introduced as the cleanup observation point.

`shmem_evict_inode` remains the backing-object retirement point.

The two lifecycle levels must remain separate.

## 10.3 Corrective implementation reported

Antigravity reported adding:

`fentry/__fput`

with `capture_fput`.

The function removes the file pointer mapping.

The inode registry remains until `shmem_evict_inode`.

Insertion rollback and error counters were also added.

This correction is architecturally necessary and should be retained.

