# 13. M2.1 Acceptance Criteria

M2.1 must not be declared complete until the following are satisfied.

## Object identity

- [ ] A correlated memfd creation receives one opaque object token.
- [ ] A successful creation transitions from provisional to committed.
- [ ] Failed or uncorrelated creation does not leave an invalid committed entry.
- [ ] Distinct memfd backing objects receive distinct tokens.
- [ ] Inode number alone is never used as the sole identity.

## Open-file registry

- [ ] Initial `struct file` is registered.
- [ ] Duplicate descriptor operations do not create duplicate unique file mappings.
- [ ] Existing token mismatches are detected.
- [ ] Genuine `/proc/self/fd/N` reopen creates a new file mapping.
- [ ] The reopened mapping resolves to the same backing-object token.
- [ ] Final `__fput` removes the unique file mapping.
- [ ] File-map deletion errors are counted.
- [ ] A file pointer reused by the kernel cannot inherit a stale association.

## Backing-object lifecycle

- [ ] Closing one descriptor does not retire the backing object while references remain.
- [ ] Reopened descriptors can continue using the same object after the original descriptor closes.
- [ ] Final backing-object eviction removes the inode registry entry.
- [ ] Exactly one retirement event is emitted for the tracked object.
- [ ] A file-description release does not prematurely retire the backing object.

## Runtime verification

- [ ] Collector runs during the controlled workload.
- [ ] Per-object tokens can be observed across relevant events.
- [ ] Counter accounting is reconciled.
- [ ] Duplication and reopen regression tests pass.
- [ ] All existing test suites pass.
- [ ] No M1 regression is introduced.

Only after these criteria pass should M2.1 be accepted and M2.2 begin.

